Package: LogicComm
Type: Package
Title: Logic-Based Cell-Cell Communication Analysis for Multi-Sample scRNA-seq
Version: 0.13.0
Date: 2026-06-10
Authors@R: person("LogicComm", "Developer", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "dev@logiccomm.io")
Author: LogicComm Developer
Maintainer: LogicComm Developer <dev@logiccomm.io>
Description: Identifies cell-cell communication signals by converting single-cell
    gene expression into Relative Expression Ordering (REO) binary logic states,
    then detecting ligand-receptor Logic Consensus Scores (LCS) from cell-type
    REO co-expression. Designed for scalable multi-sample comparison, such as case
    versus control cohorts, without requiring cell type pre-annotation. Supports
    cell-type-resolved communication summaries, signaling-role centrality with
    confidence labels, bootstrap and permutation-null diagnostics,
    receiver-response logic scoring, proliferation-confound and publication-ready
    specificity diagnostics, an axis-level permutation discovery workflow,
    sample-level quasibinomial differential modeling, role-evidence interpretation,
    rank-aware REO evidence, threshold-stability scoring, pseudotime communication
    dynamics, spatial graph and visualization utilities, report helpers,
    BPCells on-disk matrices, and Rcpp high-performance computation.
